<crash-analysis>
The crash is caused by a stack-buffer-overflow in the `pcap_findalldevs_ex` function in `pcap.c`. Specifically, at line 4758, the code attempts to access `name[stringlen - 1]` without first checking if `stringlen` is greater than 0. In the crashing test case, `stringlen` is 0, leading to an out-of-bounds read at index -1.

A patch should be applied to `pcap.c` to add a check for `stringlen > 0` before the access to `name[stringlen - 1]`.

```c
if (stringlen > 0 && name[stringlen - 1] != ENDING_CHAR) {
...
}
```
</crash-analysis>

